<title>PERU: Peru's April silver output rises 6.8 percent.</title>
<headline>Peru's April silver output rises 6.8 percent.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's silver output rose 6.8 percent to 169 tonnes in April compared with the same month last year, according to preliminary figures released Friday by the Energy and Mines Ministry.</p>
<p>Silver output rose 5.7 percent to 679 tonnes in the first four months, compared with the same period last year, the ministry added in its monthly report.</p>
<p>In 1996, silver production rose 3.1 percent to 1,968 tonnes from 1,909 tonnes.</p>
<p>Peru is the world's number two silver producer after Mexico. State-owned mining company Centromin Peru is the country's largest producer.</p>
<p>((-- Saul Hudson, Lima newsroom 511 221-2134))</p>
